        topics: ["<b style='color:var(--pc)'>\ud83d\udccb W16 (risk metrics VaR/CVaR/drawdown) = most important this week, appears in every risk interview. W17 (bonds/duration/DV01) = 1.5 days, invest here \u2014 Fixed Income QD roles (like the job spec you shared) require this. W18 (data pipelines) = half day max, you've built these.</b>", "<b style='color:var(--pc)'>\u2500\u2500 Portfolio Theory II \u2014 CAPM & Factor Models \u2500\u2500</b>", "CAPM: E[R\u1d62] = R\u1da0 + \u03b2\u1d62(E[R\u2098]\u2212R\u1da0). Expected return = risk-free rate + beta \u00d7 market risk premium. The model says you should ONLY be compensated for systematic risk \u2014 idiosyncratic risk is diversifiable and thus free to eliminate.", "Beta via OLS: \u03b2\u1d62 = Cov(R\u1d62,R\u2098)/Var(R\u2098) = the slope when regressing stock returns on market returns. Compute with scipy.stats.linregress(market_returns, stock_returns). Rolling beta: use rolling 252d windows.", "Alpha: the OLS regression intercept. \u03b1 = actual return \u2212 CAPM prediction. Positive alpha = risk-adjusted outperformance. Test if statistically significant using t-stat = \u03b1 / se(\u03b1). Most alphas are not significant.", "Fama-French 3-factor: R\u1d62 = \u03b1 + \u03b2\u2081\u00b7Mkt + \u03b2\u2082\u00b7SMB + \u03b2\u2083\u00b7HML + \u03b5. SMB = small minus big (size premium). HML = high minus low B/M (value premium). Download factor returns FREE from Ken French's data library."],
