        title: "Job Search \u2014 Amsterdam Tier 1 + EU Tier 2 (Parallel Targets)",
        topics: ["<b style='color:var(--pc)'>\ud83d\udccb You've completed Phases 1 and 2. You have a strong portfolio. Now execute. TWO parallel tracks: Amsterdam Tier 1 (Optiver/IMC/Flow Traders \u2014 the faster path to $300k+) and EU Tier 2 (Murex/BNP/London HFT firms \u2014 the safer bet). Apply to both simultaneously.</b>", "<b style='color:#F5A623'>\ud83c\udfaf TRACK A \u2014 Amsterdam Tier 1 (primary target):</b> Based on getcracked.io comp data \u2014 Optiver Amsterdam Junior Dev = $405k ($120k base + $238k bonus + $47k signing). IMC Amsterdam Junior = similar. Flow Traders = \u20ac80-130k base + bonus. As a French citizen you have full EU work rights \u2014 no visa needed. 2hr flight from Paris.", "<b>Optiver Amsterdam \u2014 interview process:</b> Stage 1 = Optigames online test (80 arithmetic problems in 8 minutes \u2014 arithmetic.zetamac.com \u2014 you've been practicing this daily since Week 1P). Stage 2 = HR + basic math phone. Stage 3 = on-site Amsterdam (trading simulation + probability deep dive + C++ technical + cultural fit). Acceptance rate ~2%.", "<b>Trading simulation prep \u2014 Optiver's trademark:</b> They give you a simple game with asymmetric information and ask you to make markets. Key insight: your bid-ask spread width = your uncertainty, not your confidence. If a jar has 50 coins (\u00b110), your market is 40-60. Practice at Jane Street's 'Figgie' game and similar.", "<b>Dutch 30% ruling:</b> As a French national working in the Netherlands for the first time, you qualify for 5 years. Effect: 30% of salary is tax-free. On \u20ac150k base: you pay income tax on \u20ac105k instead of \u20ac150k \u2014 roughly \u20ac15-20k/year extra take-home vs a Dutch national. Apply through your employer in Week 1.", "<b>IMC Amsterdam:</b> Similar to Optiver. More engineering-focused in interviews (heavier C++, system design). Compensation similar. Both are market makers \u2014 understanding market making (quoting both sides, earning the spread, managing inventory risk) is essential for interviews."],
