        topics: ["<b style='color:var(--pc)'>\ud83d\udccb Year 2. You have real QD experience. GT OMSCS in progress. Now build the specific signals US Tier 1 firms filter on. Keep working at your EU/Amsterdam firm \u2014 the experience compounds.</b>", "<b>Advanced C++ \u2014 production HFT patterns:</b> DPDK (kernel bypass networking \u2014 bypasses Linux kernel, packets go NIC\u2192application directly, adds ~1\u00b5s instead of ~5\u00b5s). FPGA basics (conceptual \u2014 sub-microsecond latency, used for order routing at Jane Street). Custom slab allocators, NUMA-aware allocation, wait-free algorithms (every thread makes progress in bounded steps).", "<b>Heston model \u2014 the industry standard vol model:</b> dS = \u03bcS dt + \u221av S dW\u2081. dv = \u03ba(\u03b8-v)dt + \u03c3\u221av dW\u2082. Corr(dW\u2081,dW\u2082) = \u03c1. Parameters: \u03ba (mean reversion), \u03b8 (long-run variance), \u03c3 (vol of vol), \u03c1 (correlation). Captures the vol smile that Black-Scholes cannot. Calibrate to market option prices.", "<b>GT OMSCS course path for QD (optimal order):</b> Semester 1: Computing for Data Analysis. Semester 2: Machine Learning. Semester 3: High Performance Computing (C++ parallel, CUDA). Semester 4: Computational Finance. Semester 5: Graduate Algorithms. Max 2 courses per semester while working full-time.", "<b>Codeforces Expert (1600) target:</b> Enter every Div 2 contest. Upsolve problems you couldn't solve. At 1600 you can reliably solve Div 2 C problems \u2014 the level US Tier 1 screens operate at. This takes ~12 months of consistent practice.", "<b>O-1A visa \u2014 start building criteria now:</b> (1) High salary at EU Tier 1 (document this). (2) Judge a hackathon or competition (arrange this). (3) Original contributions (technical blog, PreludeSDK, open source). (4) Articles (publish on arXiv \u2014 quant finance preprints accepted). (5) Critical role \u2014 get Senior QD title before applying to US."],
